The audited module now passes G1–G9(c) locally. At the hard preset it has 15 code blocks, an exact structure-aware density of \(12/29{,}216{,}880 \approx 4.11\times10^{-7}\), a 7-atom/≤22-character answer, a 285-operation compact-route bound, and a reference collision search costing up to 371,131 counted operations. The external oracle run attempted Step 4 but OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every retry, so no model failure is being misreported as hardness.
