+This is not a Track-A hardness claim.  A standard meet-in-the-middle algorithm
+forms the syndrome of every triple of columns and looks for two disjoint
+triples with the same syndrome.  It is `O(b * 36^3)` for `b` displayed blocks,
+solved 8/8 hard instances as expected, and used at most 371,131 counted
