codex
The first adversarial audit found a real weakness: the decoys all had minimum distance four, while the planted Figure‑1 code has minimum distance six. A pair-syndrome scan could therefore isolate the target before doing the weight‑six search. The paper explicitly links its electronic generator database, so I’m replacing part of the decoy pool with the paper’s classified extremal `[36,18,8]` codes; this keeps the target hidden among several blocks with no weight‑four words while preserving exact, construction-time certificates.
apply patch
