codex
Implemented a native `TRACK = "B"` generator based on the paper’s Figure‑1 self-dual `[36,18,6]` code and its [electronic code database](https://www.math.is.tohoku.ac.jp/~mharada/research/codes/sd2.htm).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1012_5464.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/gen_1012_5464.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1012.5464/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes every gate:

- Exact solution density: `12 / 31,164,672 ≈ 3.85e-7`
- Random guessing: `0/200,000`
- Four attacks: `0/8` each
- Reference algorithm: `8/8`, at most `122,645` operations
- Canonical-key tests: `100/100` invariant transformations and `20/20` distinct instances
- Answer: 7 atoms, at most 28 characters
- Intended compact route: 288 word-level operations

The external hardening verdict remains unscored: all three script-owned runs received HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before any oracle attempt completed. The raw errors are preserved, but they are not hardness evidence. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to complete Step 4.
